From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 21:32:38 +0200
Subject: ARM: sunxi: Add A13 suspend to RAM support

The A13 has no deep sleep state of its own - suspend works by putting
the DRAM into self-refresh, latching the DRAM pads (SDR_DPCR bit 0) and
cutting the SoC power rails via the AXP209, mirroring the BSP super
standby mechanism. Wakeup is a PMIC power-on event and reboots through
the bootloader SPL, which detects the pending resume via the RTC general
purpose registers and the pad hold flag, recovers the DRAM from
self-refresh and jumps to cpu_resume. Requires matching SPL support.

The final power-down sequence runs from SRAM A1 (register-only code,
TLB preloaded), because nothing in DRAM may be touched after it enters
self-refresh. A failed PMIC write backs out of self-refresh and aborts
the suspend cleanly. Always-on blocks that lose state across the power
cycle (CCU, INTC, PIO, timers, SRAM controller, the SPL DQS training
area at the start of DRAM) are saved and restored raw; peripherals are
expected to reinit their hardware in driver resume callbacks.

Signed-off-by: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
---
 arch/arm/mach-sunxi/Kconfig       |  11 +
 arch/arm/mach-sunxi/Makefile      |   1 +
 arch/arm/mach-sunxi/pm-sun5i.c    | 462 ++++++++++
 arch/arm/mach-sunxi/sleep-sun5i.S | 154 ++++
 4 files changed, 628 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm/mach-sunxi/Kconfig b/arch/arm/mach-sunxi/Kconfig
